  "body": "Bumps [solid_cable](https://github.com/rails/solid_cable) from 3.0.12 to 4.1.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/releases\">solid_cable's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.1.0</h2>\n<h1>Rails World Edition</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the channel hash directly instead of rehashing every poll by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/85\">rails/solid_cable#85</a></li>\n<li>Memoize cable configuration by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/86\">rails/solid_cable#86</a></li>\n<li>Batch writes together by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/87\">rails/solid_cable#87</a></li>\n<li>Add encryption support by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/88\">rails/solid_cable#88</a></li>\n<li>Update bench app and loadtest script by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/90\">rails/solid_cable#90</a></li>\n<li>Bring autotrimming inline with solid cache by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/89\">rails/solid_cable#89</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v4.0.2...v4.1.0\">https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v4.0.2...v4.1.0</a></p>\n<h2>v4.0.2</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reset retry counter on each successful poll by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/84\">rails/solid_cable#84</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v4.0.1...v4.0.2\">https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v4.0.1...v4.0.2</a></p>\n<h2>v4.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Run ci against different rails versions by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/79\">rails/solid_cable#79</a></li>\n<li>Update adapter to handle ActionCable adapterization in 8.2 by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/80\">rails/solid_cable#80</a></li>\n<li>Reset reconnect_attempt after successfuly accessing the DB. by <a href=\"https://github.com/pascalbetz\"><code>@​pascalbetz</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/82\">rails/solid_cable#82</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pascalbetz\"><code>@​pascalbetz</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/82\">rails/solid_cable#82</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v4.0.0...v4.0.1\">https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v4.0.0...v4.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>v4.0.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Upgrade ci to test against all ruby versions by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/76\">rails/solid_cable#76</a></li>\n<li>Drop ruby 3.1 support by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/77\">rails/solid_cable#77</a></li>\n<li>Retry if connection fails by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/75\">rails/solid_cable#75</a></li>\n<li>Eagerly initialize last_id to avoid skipping messages by <a href=\"https://github.com/xrav3nz\"><code>@​xrav3nz</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/78\">rails/solid_cable#78</a></li>\n<li>Drop ruby 3.2 support by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a></li>\n<li>Harden CI by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a></li>\n<li>Add connection timeout error and not established to the list of retryable connection errors by <a href=\"https://github.com/npezza93\"><code>@​npezza93</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/xrav3nz\"><code>@​xrav3nz</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/pull/78\">rails/solid_cable#78</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v3.0.12...v4.0.0\">https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v3.0.12...v4.0.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/1e4217e51db6e116318804776d30c3f4c2b776a4\"><code>1e4217e</code></a> disable autotrimming</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/6bb0bd443cff4f3a92d3531291a9e0954146ec8a\"><code>6bb0bd4</code></a> bump version</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/7e97e8ca670205595080ef9cfa5c2a3e37142892\"><code>7e97e8c</code></a> pass around the actual message</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/79b9839947d305a6776d13fed1178b9e33bdf338\"><code>79b9839</code></a> Pass the actual messages to broadcast_batch</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/41b1059ad6ead2f9d187b7c6ce1994e228488c34\"><code>41b1059</code></a> better naming</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/56f41fe9e8fefe8cbc19ddb321088f9dd77c6991\"><code>56f41fe</code></a> skip duping the current_channels</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/0585967705b47a3f5a0b3fef9da970fd68f68707\"><code>0585967</code></a> actually compress encrypted messages</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/a1d8b2731668beacbca8c757714f7c97ea10cc52\"><code>a1d8b27</code></a> Remove channel index since we use channel_hash now</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/c75d007d1b60c837e49852b56387e6b0a323dc69\"><code>c75d007</code></a> Bring autotrimming inline with solid cache (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/issues/89\">#89</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/commit/2dea601929ec9f27cd8752338ccab7eaa73b1dd5\"><code>2dea601</code></a> Update bench app and loadtest script (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/rails/solid_cable/issues/90\">#90</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/rails/solid_cable/compare/v3.0.12...v4.1.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=solid_cable&package-manager=bundler&previous-version=3.0.12&new-version=4.1.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>",
